# Upstream boky/postfix image runs multi-process supervisor (supervisord), crond, and rsyslog at startup,
# requiring root to configure permissions, generate postfix configuration, and manage mail queues/sockets.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0012 (Runs as root user)
KSV-0012
AVD-KSV-0012

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0001 (Can elevate its own privileges)
KSV-0001
AVD-KSV-0001

# Postfix daemons dynamically write configuration files to /etc/postfix, /tmp, and manage mail queues
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0014 (Root file system is not read-only)
KSV-0014
AVD-KSV-0014

# Postfix requires standard Unix capabilities (setuid, setgid, chown) for master process and privilege separation across daemons (smtpd, cleanup, qmgr)
# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0003 (Default capabilities: some containers do not drop all)
KSV-0003
AVD-KSV-0003

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0004 (Default capabilities: some containers do not drop any)
KSV-0004
AVD-KSV-0004

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0106 (Container capabilities must only include NET_BIND_SERVICE)
KSV-0106
AVD-KSV-0106
